# OpenHiveOS — Trivy ignore file (SEC-8)
#
# SEC-8 policy:
#   CRITICAL: 0 (no CRITICAL CVEs allowed — CI exits 1 on any CRITICAL)
#   HIGH:     managed — entries in this file must have a per-CVE justification
#             comment explaining why the CVE is acceptable and the review date.
#
# Format: <CVE-ID>  # <justification> | reviewed: <date> | next-review: <date>
#
# Instructions for adding an entry:
#   1. Confirm no fix is available (trivy reports "fixed: N/A")
#   2. Assess actual exploitability in the OpenHiveOS threat model
#   3. Add entry with required comment fields
#   4. Schedule next-review within 90 days
#   5. Locksmith signs off before merge (SEC-7 gate)
#
# BLANK FILE — no CVEs are currently suppressed.
# When the first unfixed HIGH CVE is identified, add it here with full comment.
